        "content": "Spring Framework 6.0 (used by Spring Boot 3.0) no longer matches URLs with a trailing slash by default. In Spring Boot 2.x, a controller mapped to \"/api/orders\" also answered \"/api/orders/\". After the upgrade, a request to \"/api/orders/\" returns 404 Not Found unless the trailing-slash path is mapped explicitly. Tests that call endpoints with a trailing slash start failing with \"Status expected:<200> but was:<404>\". The old behaviour can be re-enabled with PathMatchConfigurer#setUseTrailingSlashMatch(true), which is deprecated; the recommended fix is to map or redirect the trailing-slash URLs explicitly.",
